;; =======================================================
;; SCROLL-256: THE 256 WIDE DISPLAY ACROSS 64 PIXEL BLOCKS
;; =======================================================
;; The All-Stars look (a 256 wide display: fetchwid -8, ddfstrt +16, ddfstop -16, diwstrt +31, diwstop -33) played in the game showed
;; two faults the earlier proofs could not: the HUD and the menus are cut off at the left (the first part of the bitmap is not on
;; screen), and the scroll jumps about as the camera moves. proofs/sprite-attach-dual.ab3 scrolled 0 to 60 pixels only, never across a
;; 64 pixel block (where the library moves the plane pointers on and the fine delay starts again), and the fetch mode 3 block is
;; the unit of both the fetch and the delay.
;;
;; This shows it with no sprites and nothing else: the game's two lists (a 16 line HUD list of 4 planes over a dual playfield world list,
;; fetch mode 3, a world 704 wide), a ruler on each, scrolling across 0 to 384 pixels. The back playfield is a light green sky all
;; across, so the window shows as green (and the HUD band as brown) against the blue border: what is blue inside the window's own
;; edges is a part with no data.
;;
;; What the first two runs showed (2026-10-29): the fetch's start (the DDF start s) takes effect in whole 64 pixel blocks, not 16 pixel
;; steps. s 0 to 24 all put the data's start 32 pixels LEFT of the centred window (window 31), so the first 32 pixels of the bitmap are
;; cut; s 32 and above put it 32 pixels right of it (32 blank). A centred 256 window with bitmap x 0 at its left is not reachable by the
;; DDF start. Moving the window to follow the data works (displays 2 and 3 of run 2) but is not centred. s 40 and 48 jumped while
;; scrolling (the library's smooth scroll takes 8 off the start, and 40 - 8 and 48 - 8 stay in the upper block).
;;
;; Run 4 (fetch one block earlier: width 0, stop -16, start -8 to -24, window 31 and -33): scrolls properly, centred, no blue and no
;; jumps. The window's left then shows bitmap pixel X + 31 or 32 for a display x of X, so a centred 256 view needs a 32 pixel lead-in.
;;
;; This run asks whether the lead-in can be had WITHOUT a margin in the bitmaps: the bitmaps here start at world x 0 (margin 0), and
;; the display x handed to DisplayBitMap is the scroll plus a BIAS of -32 (so -32 at the left, a negative x). The window never shows
;; the bitmap's pixels left of x 0 (they are the 32 the window cuts), so if DisplayBitMap takes a negative x the bias belongs at the
;; display only. Keys 1 to 4 (all fetch width 0, stop -16, window 31 and -33):
;;   1  start -16, bias -32       2  start -16, bias -31       3  start -16, bias -33       4  start -8, bias -32
;; At scroll 0 key 1 should have the first pole and red tick at the window's left edge; 2 and 3 are one pixel either side to
;; show which is exact. If a negative x breaks (junk, a wrong picture, a wrap), the fallback is the margin of run 4.
;;
;; The rulers: the HUD band has a tick every 16 pixels of the world, its height going 1 to 8 and starting again every 128 pixels, with
;; a long red tick, 12 high, every 64; the world has a pole every 64 pixels with one box on it for the first block, two for the second
;; and so on, and a ruler of 16 pixel columns in two greens along the ground. All start at bitmap x 0.
;;
;; Keys: Right and Left scroll while held, and Space starts and stops a scroll back and forth across the whole width, at the speed
;; keys 6 to 8 set (1, 2 or 3 pixels a frame; 1 at the start); 1 to 5 the displays; Esc quits and writes scroll-256-results.txt (the
;; last display, scroll and speed).
;;
;; Run 7 (2026-10-30, from the video game/bugs/JumpyTrimmed.mp4): the jump is ONE frame, at the camera's x 32 (the display's front x crossing 0, the
;; first 64 pixel block), when everything BELOW list line 80 (#BAND_LINE, where the game's copper strings start) is drawn one block (64 px)
;; to the right and the part above is right. This adds the game's string alone: at line 79 BPLCON1 is written (CustomString, every frame)
;; with the same value the header already has (the front's and the back's fine delay, worked out as the game's UpdateBand{} does). Key 9
;; the string on (the start), key 0 off. Display 1, speed 2 or 3, Space: does the picture jump as the scroll crosses 32 (the display x 0),
;; with the string on and not with it off? R puts the scroll back to 0.
;; Result: no jump here (the proof's x is whole). The cause was in the game's band: Int(frontX*4) does not floor as the library does, so with a
;; fractional front x the band's BPLCON1 and the header disagreed by 64 pixels for one frame at a block crossing; fixed with QuarterPixels{}
;; in sparkydave.parallax.blitz.ab3 (the main project's journal notes).
;;
;; Run 6 (2026-10-30): the game shows a bigger-than-a-pixel jump of the foreground at the first scroll step of a level, only when the
;; level is started running (a camera step of 2 or more pixels a frame, from the display x -32), in 1-1 as well as 1-2. Every earlier run
;; here scrolled 1 pixel a frame. Display 1, speed 2 or 3, Space (or hold Right) from scroll 0: does the picture jump in the first
;; 64 pixels (about the first 20 frames)? At speed 1? How far does it jump, and at what scroll (the poles are 64 apart)?
;;
;; What to look at and report, for each display
;; 1. At scroll 0 (hold Left until it stops): is the one box pole (and the first red tick) at the window's left edge, in from it (how far:
;;    about how many 16 pixel ticks), or cut off? Is the green and brown area full width (16 ground columns), or short (how many)?
;; 2. Hold Right across 64, 128 and 192 (the poles): smooth, or a jump (how much, and back)? The HUD, the world and the green sky behind.
;;    Any blue at the window's left while scrolled (as the last run's second picture)?
;; 3. The right edge: junk or wrapping, or the picture short of the window's edge?
;; 4. Where does the whole picture sit on the screen: centred (the same blue each side), or to one side?

WBStartup

#RAW_KEY_ESC   = $45
#RAW_KEY_LEFT  = $4f
#RAW_KEY_RIGHT = $4e
#RAW_KEY_SPACE = $40
#RAW_KEY_R     = $13
#BPLCON1       = $102
#BAND_LINE     = 80

#HUD_YPOS   = 44
#HUD_H      = 16
#LIST_GAP   = 3
#VIEW_H     = 208
#VIEW_TOP   = 32
#WORLD_W    = 704
#WORLD_H    = 256
#HUD_W      = 704
#SCROLL_MAX = 320
#MARGIN     = 0

#HUD_FLAGS            = $13014
#WORLD_FLAGS          = $13038
#PLAYFIELD2_OFFSET_16 = $1c00
#DISPLAYS             = 4

#ADJUST_FETCHWID = -8

#BM_FRONT = 0
#BM_BACK  = 1
#BM_HUD   = 2

quitFlag.w = False
display.w = 0
Dim displayStart.w(#DISPLAYS - 1)
Dim displayDiwStart.w(#DISPLAYS - 1)
Dim displayDiwStop.w(#DISPLAYS - 1)
Dim displayFetchWid.w(#DISPLAYS - 1)
Dim displayStop.w(#DISPLAYS - 1)
Dim displayShift.w(#DISPLAYS - 1)
displayStart(0) = -16
displayStart(1) = -16
displayStart(2) = -16
displayStart(3) = -8
For displayIndex.w = 0 To #DISPLAYS - 1
  displayDiwStart(displayIndex) = 31
  displayDiwStop(displayIndex) = -33
  displayFetchWid(displayIndex) = 0
  displayStop(displayIndex) = -16
  displayShift(displayIndex) = 0
Next
displayShift(0) = -32
displayShift(1) = -31
displayShift(2) = -33
displayShift(3) = -32
scrollX.l = 0
autoScroll.w = False
autoDir.w = 1
scrollSpeed.w = 1
bandOn.w = True
keySpace.w = False
frameCount.l = 0

BitMap #BM_FRONT, #WORLD_W, #WORLD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_BACK, #WORLD_W, #WORLD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_HUD, #HUD_W, #HUD_H, 4

InitPalette 0, 32
AGAPalRGB 0, 0, 92, 148, 252
AGAPalRGB 0, 1, 156, 74, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 2, 254, 205, 198
AGAPalRGB 0, 3, 0, 0, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 4, 230, 156, 33
AGAPalRGB 0, 5, 82, 33, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 6, 140, 214, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 7, 16, 148, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 8, 255, 255, 255
AGAPalRGB 0, 9, 99, 173, 255
AGAPalRGB 0, 10, 108, 110, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 11, 255, 0, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 12, 0, 255, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 13, 76, 105, 192
AGAPalRGB 0, 14, 238, 195, 154
AGAPalRGB 0, 15, 40, 40, 40
For penIndex.w = 16 To 31
  AGAPalRGB 0, penIndex, 20 + (penIndex - 16)*6, 100 + (penIndex - 16)*6, 40 + (penIndex - 16)*3
Next

BLITZ

Statement BuildLists{}
  SHARED displayStart(), displayDiwStart(), displayDiwStop(), displayFetchWid(), displayStop()
  For displayIndex.w = 0 To #DISPLAYS - 1
    hudList.w = displayIndex*2
    worldList.w = hudList + 1
    InitCopList hudList, #HUD_YPOS, #HUD_H, #HUD_FLAGS, 0, 32, 0
    InitCopList worldList, #HUD_YPOS + #HUD_H + #LIST_GAP, #VIEW_H, #WORLD_FLAGS, 8, 0, 4
    DisplayControls worldList, 0, #PLAYFIELD2_OFFSET_16, 0
    ddfStart.w = displayStart(displayIndex)
    DisplayAdjust hudList, displayFetchWid(displayIndex), ddfStart, displayStop(displayIndex), displayDiwStart(displayIndex), displayDiwStop(displayIndex)
    DisplayAdjust worldList, displayFetchWid(displayIndex), ddfStart, displayStop(displayIndex), displayDiwStart(displayIndex), displayDiwStop(displayIndex)
  Next
End Statement

; One playfield's part of BPLCON1 for a delay of 0 to 255 quarter pixels (as sparkydave.parallax.blitz.ab3).
Function.l ScrollPart{delay.l}
  Function Return(delay AND 3)*256 + ((delay/4) AND 15) + ((delay/64) AND 3)*1024
End Function

Function.l SignedWord{value.l}
  value = value AND $ffff
  If value > 32767 Then value = value - 65536
  Function Return value
End Function

Statement ShowDisplay{displayIndex.w}
  hudList.w = displayIndex*2
  CreateDisplay hudList, hudList + 1
  DisplayPalette hudList, 0
  DisplayBitMap hudList, #BM_HUD, 0, 0
  DisplayBitMap hudList + 1, #BM_FRONT, 0, #VIEW_TOP, #BM_BACK, 0, #VIEW_TOP
End Statement

;; Poles with boxes every 64 pixels (one box for block 1, two for block 2...), 16 pixel ground columns in two greens.
Statement DrawFront{}
  Use BitMap #BM_FRONT
  Cls 0
  For columnIndex.w = 0 To #WORLD_W/16 - 1
    penIndex.w = 6
    If columnIndex MOD 2 = 1 Then penIndex = 7
    Boxf columnIndex*16, 208, columnIndex*16 + 15, 239, penIndex
  Next
  For blockIndex.w = 0 To (#WORLD_W - #MARGIN)/64 - 1
    poleX.w = #MARGIN + blockIndex*64
    Boxf poleX, 40, poleX + 1, 207, 11
    For boxIndex.w = 0 To blockIndex
      Boxf poleX + 4, 48 + boxIndex*12, poleX + 11, 55 + boxIndex*12, 8
    Next
  Next
End Statement

;; Hills on the back playfield, every circle inside the bitmap (Blitz's Circlef is not safe to clip).
Statement DrawBack{}
  Use BitMap #BM_BACK
  Cls 15
  For hillIndex.w = 0 To 9
    centreX.w = #MARGIN + 56 + hillIndex*54
    Circlef centreX, 200, 50, 2
    Circlef centreX, 200, 38, 3
    Circlef centreX, 200, 22, 4
  Next
End Statement

;; Ticks every 16 pixels of staircase height 1 to 8, repeating every 128; a long red one (12) every 64.
Statement DrawHud{}
  Use BitMap #BM_HUD
  Cls 1
  For tickIndex.w = 0 To (#HUD_W - #MARGIN)/16 - 1
    tickHeight.w = 1 + (tickIndex MOD 8)
    tickX.w = #MARGIN + tickIndex*16
    Boxf tickX, 0, tickX, tickHeight - 1, 8
    If tickIndex MOD 4 = 0 Then Boxf tickX + 1, 0, tickX + 2, 11, 11
  Next
End Statement

DrawFront{}
DrawBack{}
DrawHud{}
BuildLists{}
ShowDisplay{display}
BlitzKeys On

While quitFlag = False
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_ESC) Then quitFlag = True

  For displayKey.w = 1 To #DISPLAYS
    If RawStatus(displayKey)
      If display <> displayKey - 1
        display = displayKey - 1
        ShowDisplay{display}
      EndIf
    EndIf
  Next

  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_SPACE)
    If keySpace = False Then autoScroll = NOT autoScroll
    keySpace = True
  Else
    keySpace = False
  EndIf

  If RawStatus(9) Then bandOn = True
  If RawStatus(10) Then bandOn = False
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_R) Then scrollX = 0
  For speedKey.w = 6 To 8
    If RawStatus(speedKey) Then scrollSpeed = speedKey - 5
  Next

  If autoScroll = True
    scrollX = scrollX + autoDir*scrollSpeed
    If scrollX >= #SCROLL_MAX Then autoDir = -1
    If scrollX <= 0 Then autoDir = 1
  Else
    If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_RIGHT) AND scrollX < #SCROLL_MAX Then scrollX = scrollX + scrollSpeed
    If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_LEFT) AND scrollX > 0 Then scrollX = scrollX - scrollSpeed
  EndIf
  If scrollX < 0 Then scrollX = 0
  If scrollX > #SCROLL_MAX Then scrollX = #SCROLL_MAX

  VWait
  shiftX.w = displayShift(display)
  frontX.q = scrollX + shiftX
  backX.q = scrollX/2 + shiftX
  DisplayBitMap display*2 + 1, #BM_FRONT, frontX, #VIEW_TOP, #BM_BACK, backX, #VIEW_TOP
  DisplayBitMap display*2, #BM_HUD, frontX, 0
  ;; The game's one string, at its line: BPLCON1 with the value the header holds (no change on screen if all is well).
  If bandOn = True
    frontQuarter.l = Int(frontX*4)
    backQuarter.l = Int(backX*4)
    control.l = ScrollPart{255 - (frontQuarter AND 255)} + ScrollPart{255 - (backQuarter AND 255)}*16
    CustomString display*2 + 1, 0, #BAND_LINE - 1, Mki$(#BPLCON1) + Mki$(SignedWord{control})
  Else
    CustomString display*2 + 1, 0, #BAND_LINE - 1, Mki$($1fe) + Mki$(0)
  EndIf
  frameCount = frameCount + 1
Wend

AMIGA
If WriteFile(0, "sparky-dave:game/proofs/scroll-256-results.txt")
  FileOutput 0
  NPrint "scroll-256: the 256 wide display across 64 pixel blocks"
  NPrint "Last display ", display + 1, " (DDF start ", displayStart(display), ", window ", displayDiwStart(display), " and ", displayDiwStop(display), "), scroll ", scrollX, ", speed ", scrollSpeed, ", band string ", bandOn, ", frames ", frameCount
  CloseFile 0
EndIf
End
